{
  "_notes": [
    "Budgets for scripts/qa/check.mjs. Anything marked block fails the gate; warn is reported only.",
    "initialJsGzKB is a no-regression ceiling: the pre-redesign baseline measured 331.8KB gz, so the redesign may not add to it, and the WebGL layer must be a lazy chunk that does not count. Stretch goal worth taking separately: defer analytics (posthog) off the critical path and the ceiling drops by ~100KB. lcpMs/firstViewKB are from the same baseline plus headroom; tighten them, never loosen them, once the redesign lands.",
    "Mobile runs are CPU-throttled (cpuThrottle x). Headless Chrome uses software GL, so FPS is NOT gated here: the WebGL cost is bounded structurally (lazy chunk, pixel budget, pause-offscreen, reduced-motion, fallback) and profiled separately.",
    "sectionPages: the Figma section contract only applies to the landing page. pagesFull: the full matrix (npm run qa:full) also walks every other route, because the redesign moves them into a route group and /delete-account and /auth/callback are Play-critical.",
    "bannedClaims: regexes scanned (case-insensitive) over the landing page's text, alt and aria-label, excluding anything inside [data-disclaimer]. See docs/landing-decisions.md D1.",
    "unverified-testimonial is a warning: the owner decided to ship the Figma testimonials (docs/landing-decisions.md D2). It stays in every report.",
    "Regions (docs/landing-copy.md): the landing exists as / (US), /eu/, /gulf/ and /ru/. sectionPages are the pages that carry the Figma section contract and the claim scan. pageLang is the expected <html lang> (default en); a page must also read in that language (cyrillicShare), so a half-translated /ru/ fails.",
    "claimAllow: the narrow phrasings in which a banned word denies the claim (\"never diagnoses\", \"Does DiDi diagnose?\", Russian \"не ставит диагнозы\"). They are removed from the text before bannedClaims runs; they are not a general negation filter. unsupportedCapabilities: things the app cannot do yet (history, reports, video, comparison over time); scanned like claims, but not inside the testimonials, which are Figma placeholders (D2). placeholders: template tokens that must never reach a visitor, on every page."
  ],
